//api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/122716761","html_url":"https://github.com/g-truc/glm/issues/346#issuecomment-122716761","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/346","id":122716761,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEyMjcxNjc2MQ==","user":{"login":"Fro116","id":11019523,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDE5NTIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11019523?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116","html_url":"https://github.com/Fro116","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-07-19T23:21:13Z","updated_at":"2015-07-19T23:21:13Z","body":"Sorry, I copy/pasted the wrong code. The fixed function should really be\n\ntemplate <typename T, precision P>\nGLM_FUNC_QUALIFIER tquat<T, P> pow\n(tquat<T, P> const & x, T const & y)\n{\n\n//Raising to the power of 0 should yield 1\n\n//Needed to prevent a division by 0 error later on\nif(y > -epsilon<T>() && y < epsilon<T>())\n\n```\nreturn tquat<T, P>(1,0,0,0);\n```\n\n//To deal with non-unit quaternions\n\nT magnitude = sqrt(x.x \\* x.x + x.y \\* x.y + x.z \\* x.z + x.w *x.w);\n\n//Equivalent to raising a real number to a power\n\n//Needed to prevent a division by 0 error later on\nif(x.w / magnitude > static_cast<T>(1) - epsilon<T>() && x.w / magnitude < static_cast<T>(1) + epsilon<T>())\n\n```\nreturn tquat<T, P>(pow(x.w, y),0,0,0);\n```\n\nT Angle = acos(x.w / magnitude);\n\nT NewAngle = Angle \\* y;\nT Div = sin(NewAngle) / sin(Angle);\n\nT Mag = pow(magnitude, y-1);\n\nreturn tquat(cos(NewAngle) \\* magnitude \\* Mag, x.x \\* Div \\* Mag, x.y \\* Div \\* Mag, x.z \\* Div \\* Mag);\n}\n\nBasically, there were two problems with the original implementation: the acos line had the wrong argument, and the original implementation only worked for unit quaternions.\n\nSent from my iPhone so there may be some typos\n\n> On Jul 19, 2015, at 7:58 AM, Christophe Riccio notifications@github.com wrote:\n> \n> Hi,\n> \n> What \"sqrt(x.xx.x + x.yx.y + x.z \\* x.z);\" is supposed to do?\n> \n> This code is supposed to be equivalent to:\n> sqrt(x.x + x.x + x.z \\* x.z);\n> \n> Thanks,\n> Christophe\n> \n> —\n> Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/122716761/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Fro116","id":11019523,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDE5NTIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11019523?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116","html_url":"https://github.com/Fro116","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fro116/received_events","type":"User","user_view_